{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>you shall not spare</b> etc. — meaning that one must withhold from him everything his soul desires, even things that involve no prohibition, in order to afflict a person's soul, and he shall not spare nor take pity on him to say: why should he afflict his soul for nothing, and HaShem has permitted him these desires. Now, although this affliction falls upon the soul, its main impact is upon that which cleaves to it — namely, the forces of the inciter (מסית) that we mentioned — and this is the secret of the fast, that a person should fast to destroy the power of evil cleaving to him, which is the power of the said inciter." "And the verse's saying <b>and you shall not cover</b> — meaning, after the manner of the deed of Rav Amram the Pious (Kiddushin 81a), who cried out: ״Fire in the house of Amram!״, and they gathered together both men and women, and by this he banished the inciter (מסית) from himself. This is what is meant by <b>you shall not cover him</b> — proclaim concerning him and expose him before the eyes of all, and by this you will be delivered from him, for by this you kill him, as it says <b>for you shall surely kill him.</b>" "And the verse's saying <b>your hand shall be upon him first to put him to death</b> etc. — meaning that Scripture did not permit you to publicize his deeds and to cry out like the pious one: ״Fire in the house of Amram!״ (Kiddushin 81a), except when you are unable to manage; but when you are able to gather strength against him and repel him, you need not resort to this expedient of public exposure, but rather <b>your hand shall be upon him first to put him to death</b>, after the manner of the verse (Psalms 109:22): ״וְלִבִּי חָלַל בְּקִרְבִּי״ — and if you are unable to manage, then the hand of all the people comes last, to cry ״Fire in the house of Amram!״ so that people will come to him to kill him by their collective power, for the destruction of his desire is his death."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:15.579808193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}